<source id="1" url="https://chat.codercops.com/widget/api/" title="API Reference" section="Methods &gt; `ChatCops.update(changes)`">
API Reference > Methods > `ChatCops.update(changes)`

Change how the running chat looks or what it says, without loading it again. It takes these options from `init()`:

- `theme`, except `position`: moving the chat needs `init()`
- `branding`, `placeholder` and `strings`
- `disclosure`
- `welcomeMessage` and `suggestions`

What you leave out stays as it is, and that goes for each field inside `theme`, `branding` and `strings` too. A chat with only the welcome message shows the new one right away. Once the visitor has written, the new welcome message and suggestions wait for the next conversation. With the script tag build, a call before the chat has loaded is kept until it does, and the launcher button takes the new theme straight away.

```typescript
// A single-page app moving to its pricing page:
ChatCops.update({
  branding: { name: 'Sales', subtitle: 'Usually replies in a minute' },
  welcomeMessage: 'Questions about plans? Ask here.',
  suggestions: ['Compare plans', 'Is there a free trial?'],
});

// Following the site's own dark mode toggle:
ChatCops.update({ theme: { mode: 'dark' } });
```
</source>
<source id="2" url="https://chat.codercops.com/server/setup/" title="Server Setup" section="ChatCopsServerConfig">
Server Setup > ChatCopsServerConfig

```typescript
import type { AIProvider, Budgets, ChatCopsStorage, ChatTool, ConversationStore, KnowledgeSource, LocaleStrings, Logger, WebhookConfig } from '@chatcops/core';

interface ChatCopsServerConfig {
  // A config (see Providers for every option), or a provider object.
  provider:
    | { type: 'claude' | 'openai' | 'gemini'; apiKey: string; model?: string }
    | AIProvider;
  systemPrompt: string;
  tools?: ChatTool[];
  toolTimeoutMs?: number;
  maxTokens?: number;
  temperature?: number;
  knowledge?: KnowledgeSource[];
  budgets?: Budgets | false;   // on by default, see Budgets below
  preChatFields?: string[];   // pre-chat form fields to keep; kept from the first message on
  rateLimit?: {
    maxRequests: number;
    windowMs: number;
  };
  webhooks?: WebhookConfig[];
  analytics?: boolean;
  storage?: ChatCopsStorage;            // where conversations, counters and locks live
  retention?: { conversationsDays?: number };   // for purge(); default 30
  /** @deprecated Use `storage`. */
  conversationStore?: ConversationStore;
  allowedOrigins?: string[];   // default ['*']
  /** @deprecated Use `allowedOrigins`. */
  cors?: string;
  clientIp?: (request: Request) => string | null | undefined;   // fetch handlers, see the fetch runtimes page
  sessionSecrets?: string[];   // turns on session tokens, see Session tokens below
  sessionTtlSec?: number;      // default 900
  requireSession?: boolean;    // default true when sessionSecrets is set
  turnstile?: { secretKey: string; action?: string; expectedHostnames?: string[]; timeoutMs?: number };
  identity?: { secret: string; tiers?: Record<string, Budgets> };   // signed-in visitors, see below
  exposeUsage?: boolean;   // token usage in protocol v1 finish parts; default false
  logger?: Logger;         // where notes and errors go, see Logging below; default consoleLogger()
  /** @deprecated Ignored by the server. Use the widget's `strings` option. */
  i18n?: {
    defaultLocale: string;
    locales: Record<string, LocaleStrings>;
  };
}
```
</source>
<source id="3" url="https://chat.codercops.com/" title="ChatCops Documentation" section="Architecture">
ChatCops Documentation > Architecture

```
┌──────────────────┐         ┌──────────────────┐
│   Your Website   │  SSE    │   Your Server    │
│                  │ ──────► │                  │
│  <script> tag    │ ◄────── │  @chatcops/server│
│  @chatcops/widget│ stream  │  ├─ Provider     │
│  Shadow DOM      │         │  ├─ Knowledge    │
│  Chat Panel      │         │  ├─ Tools        │
└──────────────────┘         │  └─ Analytics    │
                             └──────────────────┘
```
</source>
<source id="4" url="https://chat.codercops.com/examples/vercel-full/" title="Vercel Edge Full Example" section="API Route (`api/chat.ts`)">
Vercel Edge Full Example > API Route (`api/chat.ts`)

```typescript
import { chatcopsVercelHandler } from '@chatcops/server';
import { LeadCaptureTool, FAQKnowledgeSource } from '@chatcops/core';

export const config = { runtime: 'edge' };

export default chatcopsVercelHandler({
  provider: {
    type: 'claude',
    apiKey: process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY!,
    model: 'claude-haiku-5-5',
  },

  systemPrompt: `You are a helpful AI assistant for our SaaS product.
    Answer questions about features, pricing, and getting started.
    If a user shares contact info, capture it with the lead tool.`,

  tools: [
    new LeadCaptureTool(async (lead) => {
      // Send to webhook (e.g., Zapier, Make, n8n)
      await fetch(process.env.WEBHOOK_URL!, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({
          type: 'lead_captured',
          lead,
          timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
        }),
      });
    }),
  ],

  knowledge: [
    new FAQKnowledgeSource([
      { question: 'What is your pricing?', answer: 'Starter: Free, Pro: $29/mo, Enterprise: Custom.' },
      { question: 'Is there a free trial?', answer: 'Yes, 14-day free trial on all paid plans.' },
      { question: 'What integrations do you support?', answer: 'Slack, Discord, Zapier, webhooks, and REST API.' },
    ]),
  ],

  allowedOrigins: ['*'],
  analytics: true,
});
```
</source>
<source id="5" url="https://chat.codercops.com/server/ai-sdk/" title="AI SDK (useChat)">
AI SDK (useChat)

`chatcopsAiSdkHandler` answers in the [AI SDK](https://ai-sdk.dev)'s UI message stream, so an app that already uses `useChat` can use a ChatCops server instead of its own route. You keep your chat UI and get ChatCops on the server: stored conversations, rate limits, budgets, allowed origins and tools.

It's a Fetch API handler like `chatcopsVercelHandler`, so it works as a Next.js route handler and in any runtime from the [fetch runtimes page](/server/fetch-runtimes/). It's tested against `ai` 7.
</source>
</sources>

